  "prefLabel": "Bea 502.27 Land use regulations and ordinances",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Bea 502.27 “Land use regulations and ordinances” means rules regulating how land might be used, including, but is not limited to, zoning ordinances adopted pursuant to RSA 674:16, innovative land use controls adopted pursuant to RSA 674:21, subdivision regulations adopted pursuant to RSA 674:35, and site plan regulations adopted pursuant to RSA 674:43.\n\nSource. #14043, eff 8-8-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/bea500.html"
